---
import Img from './Img.astro';
const {city} = Astro.props as {city:'miami'|'panama-city'};
const miami=city==='miami';
---
<section class="p-band"><div class="wrap local-intro">
  <div><span class="kick">{miami?'Miami / Florida':'Panama City / Florida'}</span><h2 class="disp p-sec">{miami?'Make the business clear. Make the reporting useful.':'Close to the work. Clear on the numbers.'}</h2></div>
  <div class="p-body">
    {miami ? <><p>ZINC serves Miami businesses with AI-search optimization, business intelligence and the websites behind them. The starting point is the decision you need to improve: how customers find you, whether your offer is represented accurately, or why your reports disagree.</p><p>We work from our principal base in Panama City and serve clients in Miami. Start with an inquiry to agree on scope and meeting arrangements.</p></> : <><p>Panama City is ZINC’s principal current operating base. We help businesses make their services easier to understand in search and turn operational records into useful reporting.</p><p>For a business serving the waterfront, managing field visits or selling across several channels, the work starts with the actual customer journey and the records available. A dashboard or an AI-search citation is useful only when it helps the business make a better decision.</p></>}
  </div>
</div></section>
<section class="p-band"><div class="wrap local-services">
  <article><span class="kick">Demand</span><h2>AI-search optimization</h2><p>Check how your business is described, whether its important pages can be discovered, and whether its claims have supporting evidence. Improve the answers buyers need and observe citations with their sampling limits stated.</p><ul><li>Business identity and source consistency</li><li>Service-aligned article categories and useful answers</li><li>Crawl, indexing and structured-data checks</li><li>Documented search observations and inquiry measurement</li></ul><a href="/services/ai-search-optimization/">Explore generative search optimization</a></article>
  <article><span class="kick">Intelligence</span><h2>Business intelligence</h2><p>Start with one decision and the records needed to support it. Agree on definitions before combining reports, then build a view your team can check and use.</p><ul><li>Source and access requirements</li><li>KPI definitions, dates and exclusions</li><li>Reporting tied to operational decisions</li><li>Source reconciliation and clear handover</li></ul><a href="/services/business-intelligence/">Explore business intelligence</a></article>
</div></section>
<section class="p-band"><div class="wrap"><figure class="local-work"><Img k={miami?'felon-web-mockup':'smd-brand-book'} alt={miami?'Website creative designed for Felon Motorwerk':'Summit Marine Development brand identity designed by ZINC'} sizes="(max-width:760px) 100vw, 80vw" /><figcaption>{miami?'Felon Motorwerk / Website and brand applications':'Summit Marine Development / Brand identity'}</figcaption></figure></div><div class="wrap local-intro">
  <div><span class="kick">Relevant work</span><h2 class="disp p-sec">{miami?'Miami brands, made tangible.':'A Panama City business, built across channels.'}</h2></div>
  <div class="p-body">{miami ? <><p>For Felon Motorwerk, ZINC’s work included brand and campaign design, mockups, apparel and tag printing, in-store graphics, merchandising, color and customer flow. Miami Tactical’s project included website and logo design.</p><p><a href="/work/felon-motorwerk/">Felon Motorwerk</a> · <a href="/work/miami-tactical/">Miami Tactical</a></p></> : <><p>Summit Marine Development’s scope connects its website, brand identity and local marketing. The case study includes logo development, brand materials, website presentations and campaign creative for its waterfront construction business.</p><p><a href="/work/summit-marine-development/">See Summit Marine Development</a></p></>}</div>
</div></section>
<section class="p-band"><div class="wrap local-intro">
  <div><span class="kick">Before the first conversation</span><h2 class="disp p-sec">Bring the question.</h2></div>
  <div class="p-body"><p>Tell us which service or decision matters, what is failing today and which systems hold the relevant information. Share public URLs first; account access and private records can be agreed after scope is clear.</p><p>For AI search, bring the questions customers ask and the pages that should answer them. For BI, bring the definitions behind the reports that disagree. We will identify what can be checked, what is missing and what a first useful delivery should include.</p><p>Website, ecommerce and SEO work can support either engagement when the underlying customer journey needs repair. Scope and responsibilities are agreed before implementation.</p><p><a href="/contact/">Start an inquiry</a></p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="p-band"><div class="wrap"><span class="kick">Read before you commission</span><div class="local-reading"><a href="/blog/ai-search-results-and-generative-search-optimization/">What AI-search visibility actually involves</a><a href="/blog/business-intelligence-basics/">Define the reporting decision first</a><a href="/blog/build-a-content-hub-people-can-use/">Organize useful content around your services</a><a href="/blog/category/ai-search-optimization/">Browse AI-search articles</a><a href="/blog/category/business-intelligence/">Browse business-intelligence articles</a><a href={'/locations/'+(miami?'panama-city':'miami')+'/'}>{miami?'Our Panama City work':'Services for Miami businesses'}</a></div></div></section>
<style>
.local-work{margin:0 0 3rem}.local-work :global(img){display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:640px;object-fit:contain}.local-work figcaption{font-size:.875rem;margin-top:1rem}.local-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,1.15fr);gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,6rem)}
.local-services{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,7rem)}
.local-services article{border-top:1px solid var(--line,#777);padding-top:2rem;min-width:0}.local-services h2{font-size:clamp(1.8rem,3vw,3rem);line-height:1.12;margin:1rem 0}.local-services p,.local-services li{font-size:1.125rem;line-height:1.7}.local-services ul{padding-left:1.25rem;margin:1.5rem 0}.local-reading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:0 3rem;margin-top:1.5rem}.local-reading a{padding:1.4rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#777);font-size:1.2rem}.p-body p+p{margin-top:1.25rem}
@media(max-width:760px){.local-intro,.local-services,.local-reading{grid-template-columns:1fr}.local-intro{gap:1.5rem}.local-services{gap:3rem}}
</style>
